I've committed the change. The top-level mcp = [...] list is now read straight from the parsed TOML, and the hand-written array reader that used to re-read it has no production callers left. Users see no difference. Format, clippy (-D warnings), the full cargo test run, the module-size gate and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

What changed
• The old path: the toml crate parsed mcp, the config loader turned it back into text, and parse_toml_array (the hand parser) parsed that text again.
• The new path: config::parse_mcp_list_from_config reads the list from the parsed table, in a new function in config_toml_read.rs. Both places that read mcp use it: startup in cli.rs (parse_mcp_and_openapi_config, which also lost a parameter it no longer used) and cd_config_note.rs.
• Same file as before: at the startup call site, the settings map and the raw config text come from the same loaded file, so where mcp comes from hasn't changed.

How I checked that nothing changed for users
• A new test runs the old path and the new reader on 11 inputs and they agree on all of them. The inputs are: two commands, a command containing , , a multi-line list with comments, an empty list, no mcp key, an empty file, mcp = "x", mcp = [1, true], a nested list, a [mcp] table, and invalid TOML.
• Recall control: with the new reader neutered (marker count confirmed as 1 before the run), both new tests failed by name. After restoring it they passed. No older test caught the neutered reader, so before this change nothing tested the mcp list on its own.

#1184's measure of what's left: the line-by-line reading count went from 12 to 11, and parse_toml_array production callers from 2 to 0. I posted the before and after numbers on #1184 as I took them.

Left on #1184 (so the commit says "Part of", not "Fixes"):
• parse_toml_array is now marked test-only. Its tests in cli.rs, config.rs and config_toplevel_tests.rs need moving to the new reader before it can be deleted.
• The line-by-line readers in config_value.rs and config_unknown_keys.rs are still there.
• The differential test that checks my parser against Python's TOML parser still has to be deleted.

Also worth knowing
• My first try made parse_toml_array available to tests with a test-only line at the top of cli.rs. That broke restricted::only_one_place_decides_whether_the_run_is_restricted, because that test splits cli.rs at the first #[cfg(test)] and assumes everything above it is production code. I removed that line and pointed the cli.rs tests at crate::config::parse_toml_array instead.
• I added an ARCHITECTURE.md entry noting that two older entries still name parse_toml_array as the mcp reader and are now out of date.
• config.rs grew 7 lines to 4555, which is still inside the size gate's allowance, so I didn't change its entry in tests/module_size.rs.
